    buf_bytes(out, b"read_stdin_in(gpa) -> Result<Vec<u8, Gpa>, IoError> all of stdin\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"print(x), println(x)             any Display; println(\"{x} {:?}\", v)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"b.push_int(v: i64)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.set(i: usize, x: T)            checked, as v[i] = x\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"Scanner::new(text: [u8]) -> Scanner\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"sc.next_int() -> Result<i64, ScanError>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"o.unwrap_or(x: T) -> T           Option, Result\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.clear()                        Vec, Buf\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.sort()                         by Ord: numbers, [u8], tuples, #[derive(Eq, Ord)]\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.sort_by(|a, b| a.x - b.x)      a, b: let T (a - b); < 0: a first; cmp_of(a, b)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"HashMap::new_in(gpa) -> HashMap<K, V>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.pop() -> Option<T>             v.remove(i: usize) -> T; m.remove(k) -> Option<V>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"Vec::filled_in(n: usize, x: T, gpa) -> Vec<T>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"sort(s: inout [T])               a slice in place: sort(&v[a..b]), v.sort()\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"for (k, x) in m.iter()           in slot order (not insertion order)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"m.get_or_insert(k: K, d: V) -> inout [V]   m.get_or_insert(w, 0)[0] += 1;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"sc.next_token() -> Option<[u8]>  sc.next_line() -> Option<[u8]>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"parse_int(s: [u8]) -> Result<i64, ParseIntError>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"m.insert(k: K, x: V) -> Option<V>     Vec: v.insert(i: usize, x: T)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"std::print_int(v: i64)           std::is_digit(b: u8) -> bool\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"trim(s: [u8]) -> [u8]\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"read_line(&s) -> Result<bool, IoError>    Ok(false) at the end of input\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"split_whitespace_in(s: [u8], gpa) -> Vec<[u8]>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"split_in(s: [u8], sep: u8, gpa) -> Vec<[u8]>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.swap(i: usize, j: usize)       m.contains_key(k: K) -> bool\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"MinHeap::new_in(gpa), h.push(x), h.pop() -> Option<T>   a priority queue, smallest first; BinaryHeap: largest\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`[u8]` compares with `==`, `<` and `cmp_of` (`'a'` is a `u8`); `for b\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"in s` yields its bytes. A slice from `as_slice()`, `trim`, `split_in` or\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"a `Scanner` views its text: keep the `Buf`, and push to it only when\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"done with them (`guide std#overview`).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"An allocator (`gpa`, from `fn main(gpa: Gpa)`, passed down as a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"parameter) goes only to constructors and `_in` functions; methods\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(`push`, `insert`, `clone`, `sort`) use the container's own. Not in\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"std: `Box`. (0.20) Text: `str`, `String` and Rust's methods (`guide\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"text`); files, env, processes: `guide io`. (0.20)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`std::collections::HashSet`: `insert` (false if present), `contains`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`remove`, `iter()`. `BTreeMap<K, V>` and `BTreeSet<T>`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(`std::BTreeMap`, `K: Ord`) keep their keys in order: `iter()` and\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`range(lo, hi)` (`[lo, hi)`; `range_inclusive`) go from the smallest,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`next_back()` from the largest; `first_key_value`, `pop_first`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`pop_last`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"@PAGE-END@ More, a section at a time: `volec guide std#the-api` (every item, a line each), `std#overview` (ownership, views, HashMap), `std#input` (reading stdin), `std#heaps` (priority queues); one item: `volec guide --find NAME`; all of it: `volec guide std --whole`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## Overview\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"The standard library is the module `std`, built into the compiler. The\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"prelude names need no import: `Option`, `Some`, `None`, `Result`, `Ok`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`Err`, `Vec`, `print`, `println`, `eprint`, `eprintln`, `format`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`format_in`, the allocators (`Gpa`, `Allocator`, `Arena`, `ScopedArena`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`arena_scope`), the traits `Add`, `Sub`, `Mul`, `Div`, `Neg`, `Eq`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`Ord`, `Hash`, `Iterator`, `Display`, `Debug`, `Clone`, `From`, `Into`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"and (0.17) `Buf`, `HashMap`, `read_line`, `read_stdin_in`, `Scanner`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`parse_int`, `trim`, `split_in`, `split_whitespace_in`, `sort`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`sort_by`, `sort_stable`, `sort_stable_by` (and their `_in` forms),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`cmp_of`, `eq_of`, `Fmt`, `panic(msg)` and `unreachable()`; (0.18.1)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"the heaps `BinaryHeap` and `MinHeap`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"Anything else is used by path (`std::print_int(n)`) or imported by name\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(`use std::{IoError, is_digit};`).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"What a Rust programmer will miss: there is no `String` (use `[u8]` and\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`Buf`), no file reading (call C; iterators: `volec guide\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"iterators`). A `Vec` (and a `Buf`) indexes as\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"its slice: `v[i]`, `v[i] = x`, `v[a..b]` (0.17), checked. Formatting is Rust's,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`println(\"{x:>4}\")` (`volec guide formatting`); errors are enums in a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`Result` (`volec guide conversions`). A `Vec`, `Buf` or `HashMap` is\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"dropped (freed) at the end of its scope (0.17): no `free` calls.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `Vec<T, A>`, `Buf` and `HashMap<K, V, A>` own their memory: `let w = v;`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  moves it, `.clone()` copies. A function that reads one takes it\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  let (`v: Vec<T, A>`, called `f(v)`: borrowed), one that changes it\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `v: inout Vec<T, A>` (called `f(&v)`), one that keeps it `v: sink\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  Vec<T, A>` (`f(v)` moves it).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- A slice from `as_slice()` views the container: the checker rejects its\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  use after the next push, `free` or drop (`volec guide views`).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `get`, `set`, slice indexing and `unwrap` are checked: a failure prints\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  a message and exits with 101.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `HashMap` keys need `Hash` and `Eq` (integers, `bool`, `[u8]` have\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  them; for a struct key, write `impl Hash`; `==` is structural). `==` on\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  Vecs, Bufs and maps compares their contents (0.15). `get`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  returns a copy of the value in an `Option`. Iterate with\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `for i in 0..m.slots()` and `key_at(i)`/`value_at(i)`, in slot order\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  (not the order of insertion).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- (0.20) A `HashMap` is a Swiss table (hashbrown's design), and std's\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  hashes are foldhash with fixed seeds (`std::hash::FixedState`): the\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  slot order is the same in every run and on every target. Not proof\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  against keys an attacker chooses: `std::hash::SipHashState::new()`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  hashes with SipHash-1-3 and random keys, as Rust's default does.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- To change a value in place, `get_mut(k)` and `get_or_insert(k, d)`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  give a writable view of one element (`inout [V]`; `a[0]` is the value),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  safe to use until the map's next insert, remove or free, like\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `as_mut_slice()`: Rust's `*m.entry(k).or_insert(0) += 1` is\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `counts.get_or_insert(word, 0)[0] += 1;`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `sort(s)` sorts a slice in place by `Ord` (an introsort: O(n log n),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  not stable); `v.sort()`, `s.sort()` too.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- (0.17) `sort(&a[..])`, `sort(v.as_mut_slice())`; `v.free()`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  frees now and leaves `v` empty; `v.take()` moves the contents out,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  leaving an empty container with the same allocator;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `std::take(&x)`, `std::replace(&x, v)`, `std::swap(&a, &b)`;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `v.iter_ref()` yields let accesses of the elements.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```vole\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn main(gpa: Gpa) -> i32 {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var counts: HashMap<[u8], i64, Gpa> = HashMap::new_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let words = [\"a\", \"b\", \"a\", \"c\", \"a\"];\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    for w in words {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        counts.get_or_insert(w, 0)[0] += 1;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    if let Some(n) = counts.get_mut(\"c\") {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        n[0] *= 10;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    for i in 0..counts.slots() {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        if let Some(k) = counts.key_at(i) {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"            print(k);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"            print(\"=\");\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"            std::print_int(counts.value_at(i).unwrap());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"            print(\" \");\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"\");\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    std::print_int(counts.len() as i64);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    if counts.contains_key(\"b\") { println(\" has b\"); }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    0\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```out\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"b=1 a=3 c=10\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"3 has b\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## Heaps: priority queues\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`BinaryHeap<T>` and `MinHeap<T>` (`T: Ord`; tuples compare field by\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"field) are priority queues: `push(x)`, `pop() -> Option<T>`, `peek()`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`len()`, `from_vec(v)`, `into_sorted_vec()`; a BinaryHeap pops the\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"largest first, a MinHeap the smallest (Rust's `BinaryHeap<Reverse<T>>`:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"vole has no tuple structs, so no `Reverse(x)`). Dijkstra with a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"MinHeap: `volec guide --find dijkstra`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## Input\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`read_line(&buf)` reads stdin a line at a time: the line goes into the\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`String` without its `'\\n'`, and the result is `Ok(false)` at the end of\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"input (an empty line is `Ok(true)` with an empty `buf`; a read error is\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`Err(IoError::Read)`). `read_stdin_in(gpa)` returns the rest of stdin (a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`Result<Vec<u8, Gpa>, IoError>`); the two share a buffer: they mix, but\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"not with C's `getchar`. A `Scanner` reads a text's tokens\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(`next_token`; `next_int`, a `Result<i64, ScanError>`) and lines\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(`next_line`); `parse_int` (a `Result<i64, ParseIntError>`),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`split_in`, `split_whitespace_in` and `trim` work on any `[u8]`. An Option\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"means absence (the end, nothing found), a Result a failure: `.ok()`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"turns one into the other, `.unwrap_or(x)` gives a default. What they\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"return are views of the text: keep the line until done with them. The\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"next `read_line` overwrites the line, so to keep a part of it (a map's\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"key), read all of stdin and take lines with `Scanner::next_line`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```vole\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn main(gpa: Gpa) -> i32 {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var line = String::new_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    read_line(&line).unwrap();            // the header: \"n m\"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let header = split_whitespace_in(line.as_slice(), gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let n = parse_int(header.get(0)).unwrap();\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let m = parse_int(header.get(1)).unwrap_or(0);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let rest = read_stdin_in(gpa).unwrap(); // everything after it\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var sc = Scanner::new(rest.as_slice());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var sum = 0;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    for _ in 0..n {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        sum += sc.next_int().unwrap();\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    std::print_int(sum * m);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    print(\" [\");\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    print(sc.next_line().unwrap());       // the rest of that line\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"]\");\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    while let Some(l) = sc.next_line() {  // the lines after it\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        print(l);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        println(\"|\");\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    0\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```in\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"3 2\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"10 20 30 tail\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"x y\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"last\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```out\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"120 [ tail]\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"x y|\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"|\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"last|\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## The API\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"Generated from std's source in this compiler: every public item a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"program uses, one line each, in std's source spelling (`self` reads;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`inout self` changes, called as `v.push(x)` on a `var`; `sink self`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"takes the value). Each item with its\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"comment: `volec guide std#every-item`; one item's source: `volec\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"query show std::Scanner::next_line`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```text\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"@STD-API@\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"@STD-API-DOC@\n");
}
